        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Counterclockwise on medium or high in summer, and raise the thermostat while it runs. Clockwise on the lowest speed in winter, and only in rooms tall enough to trap warm air. Check the setting with the breeze test, not by squinting at blurred blades.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your fan cannot make a breeze worth having in either direction, the setting is not the problem. Size the replacement to the room and pick one you can reverse from the couch; our <a href="/best-ceiling-fans-with-lights/" class="text-[#38BDF8]">tested ceiling fan picks</a> are the place to start.
